/*!
  \page example_cu_ssc_page Screen-space curvature using CUDA/C++

  \section cu_ssgl_intro_sec Introduction

  This example computes the screen-space curvature \cite Mellado:2013:SSC of images storing, for each pixel, a
  position and a normal (e.g. the G-buffers of a deferred renderer). Each CUDA thread fits an algebraic sphere with
  the GLS parameters in a screen-space neighborhood of its pixel, and outputs the curvature \f$\kappa\f$.

  \subsection cu_ssgl_sec_dep_subsec Installation and usage

  The example requires CUDA (12 or later) and libpng. To compile and run it:
  \code{.sh}
  cmake --build build --target ponca_ssgls
  cd build/examples/cuda/ssgls && ./ponca_ssgls
  \endcode

  The program reads the two input pictures of the `data` folder (copied next to the executable), computes the
  curvature for a screen-space neighborhood of radius 10 pixels, and writes the result in `ssgls_results.png`.
  \image html examples/ssgls_input.png "Screen-space curvature, typical input. Left: world coordinates. Right: remapped normal vectors"

  It generates this picture:
  \image html examples/ssgls_result1.png "Screen-space curvature estimation"

  \section cu_ssgl_cuda_sec CUDA programming

  The technical details related to the CUDA and C++ binding for screen-space curvature estimation are as follows.

  \subsection cu_ssgl_cuda_mypoint_sec Fitting data structure
  The point type stores a position, a normal and screen-space coordinates:
  \snippet cuda/ssgls/ponca_ssgls.cu mypoint

  \subsection cu_ssgl_cuda_weight_sec Weighting function
  The neighbor filter weights the neighbors according to their screen-space distance:
  \snippet cuda/ssgls/ponca_ssgls.cu w_def

  \subsection cu_ssgl_cuda_fit_sec Fitting primitive
  \snippet cuda/ssgls/ponca_ssgls.cu fit_def

  \subsection cu_ssgl_cuda_kernel_sec Kernel
  \snippet cuda/ssgls/ponca_ssgls.cu kernel

  \subsection cu_ssgl_cuda_access_sec Memory access
  The input data are stored by dimension (in object space), then by screen-space coordinates:
  \snippet cuda/ssgls/ponca_ssgls.cu data_acces

  \section cu_ssgl_sec Source code
  The images are read and written with libpng.

  \include cuda/ssgls/ponca_ssgls.cu
